          "eligibilityDescription_md": "\n1. The applicant must be a resident of Uttarakhand.\n1. The applicant must be a woman.\n1. The applicant must be from one of the following categories:\n\n\n- Abandoned\n- Widow\n- Destitute\n- Single woman\n- Disaster-affected woman\n\n<br>\n\n"
        },
        "schemeContent": {
          "benefitTypes": {
            "id": 1,
            "label": "Cash",
            "value": "cash"
          },
          "benefits": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Under this scheme, one unit of goats (3 females and 1 male) aged 12 to 18 months is provided to eligible women. The entire cost of the scheme, ₹35,000, is borne by the State Government."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "type": "align_justify"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "benefits_md": "Under this scheme, one unit of goats (3 females and 1 male) aged 12 to 18 months is provided to eligible women. The entire cost of the scheme, ₹35,000, is borne by the State Government.\n<br>\n\n",
          "briefDescription": "The scheme aims to empower women, especially abandoned, widowed, destitute, single, and disaster-affected women, by providing them support for goat rearing to generate livelihood and improve household income.",
          "detailedDescription": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The scheme \"Mahila Bakri Palan\" was introduced by the Department of Animal Husbandry, Government of Uttarakhand. The scheme aims to empower women, especially abandoned, widowed, destitute, single, and disaster-affected women, by providing them support for goat rearing to generate livelihood and improve household income."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "type": "align_justify"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "detailedDescription_md": "The scheme &amp;quot;Mahila Bakri Palan&amp;quot; was introduced by the Department of Animal Husbandry, Government of Uttarakhand. The scheme aims to empower women, especially abandoned, widowed, destitute, single, and disaster-affected women, by providing them support for goat rearing to generate livelihood and improve household income.\n<br>\n\n",
